","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":109},{"base":"H6242","lemma":"עֶשְׂרִים","tr":"es·rim","gloss":"twenty","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":315},{"base":"H3086","lemma":"יְהוֹעַדָּן","tr":"ye·ho·ad·din","gloss":"Jehoaddan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3371","lemma":"יׇקְתְאֵל","tr":"yoq·te·el","gloss":"Joktheel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":24,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"Fathers shall not be put to death for their children, nor children for their fathers; each is to die for his own sin.","from":6},{"book":"EZK","chapter":18,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"The soul who sins is the one who will die. A son will not bear the iniquity of his father, and a father will not bear the iniquity of his son. The righteousness of the righteous man will fall upon him, and the wickedness of the wicked man will fall upon him.","from":6},{"book":"EZK","chapter":18,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"Behold, every soul belongs to Me; both father and son are Mine. The soul who sins is the one who will die.","from":6},{"book":"JER","chapter":31,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Instead, each will die for his own iniquity. If anyone eats the sour grapes, his own teeth will be set on edge.","from":6},{"book":"2SA","chapter":8,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And David made a name for himself when he returned from striking down eighteen thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt.","from":7},{"book":"2KI","chapter":12,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Nevertheless, the high places were not removed; the people continued sacrificing and burning incense there.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Whoever sheds the blood of man, by man his blood will be shed; for in His own image God has made mankind.","from":5},{"book":"EXO","chapter":21,"verse":12,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Whoever strikes and kills a man must surely be put to death. If, however, he did not lie in wait, but God allowed it to happen, then I will appoint for you a place where he may flee. But if a man schemes and acts willfully against his neighbor to kill him, you must take him away from My altar to be put to death.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"8-16":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":7,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"joash-h3101j","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":6,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"amaziah-h0558g","name":"Amaziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":5,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jehoahaz-h3059g","name":"Jehoahaz","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jehu-h3058h","name":"Jehu","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":6,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"ahaziah-h0274h","name":"Ahaziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"joash-h3101i","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379h","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"places":[{"id":"lebanon-h3844g","name":"Lebanon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"edom-h0123g","name":"Edom","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"beth-shemesh-h1053g","name":"Beth-shemesh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"corner-gate-h6438g","name":"Corner Gate","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"ephraim-gate-h0669h","name":"Ephraim Gate","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"samaria-h8111","name":"Samaria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"H3060","lemma":"יְהוֹאָשׁ","tr":"ye·ho·ash","gloss":"Jehoash","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":17},{"base":"H0558","lemma":"אֲמַצְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"a·mats·yah","gloss":"Amaziah","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":40},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":820},{"base":"H1053","lemma":"בֵּית שֶׁ֫מֶשׁ","tr":"bet she·mesh","gloss":"Beth-shemesh","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":42},{"base":"H3844","lemma":"לְבָנוֹן","tr":"le·va·non","gloss":"Lebanon","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":71},{"base":"H2336","lemma":"חוֹחַ","tr":"cho·ach","gloss":"thistle","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1051},{"base":"H7971","lemma":"שָׁלַח","tr":"sha·lach","gloss":"to send: depart","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":847},{"base":"H8111","lemma":"שֹׁמְרוֹן","tr":"sho·me·ron","gloss":"Samaria","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":109},{"base":"H8594","lemma":"תַּעֲרֻבָה","tr":"ta·a·ru·vah","gloss":"security","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":8,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"then your heart will become proud, and you will forget the LORD your God who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery.","from":10},{"book":"JDG","chapter":9,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"One day the trees set out to anoint a king for themselves. They said to the olive tree, ‘Reign over us.’","from":9},{"book":"JDG","chapter":9,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"But the thornbush replied, ‘If you really are anointing me as king over you, come and find refuge in my shade. But if not, may fire come out of the thornbush and consume the cedars of Lebanon.’","from":9},{"book":"2CH","chapter":26,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But when Uzziah became powerful, his arrogance led to his own destruction. He was unfaithful to the LORD his God, for he entered the temple of the LORD to burn incense on the altar of incense.","from":10},{"book":"NEH","chapter":8,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And the people went out, brought back branches, and made booths on their own rooftops, in their courtyards, in the court of the house of God, and in the squares by the Water Gate and by the Gate of Ephraim.","from":13},{"book":"EXO","chapter":8,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Moses said to Pharaoh, “You may have the honor over me. When shall I pray for you and your officials and your people that the frogs (except for those in the Nile) may be taken away from you and your houses?”","from":10},{"book":"JOS","chapter":19,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Iron, Migdal-el, Horem, Beth-anath, and Beth-shemesh. There were nineteen cities, along with their villages.","from":11},{"book":"JOS","chapter":21,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Ain, Juttah, and Beth-shemesh—nine cities from these two tribes, together with their pasturelands.","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"17-22":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":4,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"amaziah-h0558g","name":"Amaziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"jehoahaz-h3059g","name":"Jehoahaz","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"joash-h3101i","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"joash-h3101j","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"uzziah-h5818g","name":"Uzziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"lachish-h3923","name":"Lachish","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"elath-h0359a","name":"Elath","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22}],"words":[{"base":"H0558","lemma":"אֲמַצְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"a·mats·yah","gloss":"Amaziah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":40},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":820},{"base":"H3923","lemma":"לָכִישׁ","tr":"la·khish","gloss":"Lachish","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"H0310","lemma":"אַחַר","tr":"a·char","gloss":"after","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":715},{"base":"H6240","lemma":"עָשָׂר","tr":"a·sar","gloss":"ten","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":337},{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":643},{"base":"H0359","lemma":"אֵילַת","tr":"e·lat","gloss":"Elath","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":877},{"base":"H7195","lemma":"קֶ֫שֶׁר","tr":"qe·sher","gloss":"conspiracy","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H3060","lemma":"יְהוֹאָשׁ","tr":"ye·ho·ash","gloss":"Jehoash","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":16,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"At that time Rezin king of Aram recovered Elath for Aram, drove out the men of Judah, and sent the Edomites into Elath, where they live to this day.","from":22},{"book":"1KI","chapter":9,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"King Solomon also assembled a fleet of ships at Ezion-geber, which is near Eloth in Edom, on the shore of the Red Sea.","from":22},{"book":"DEU","chapter":2,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So we passed by our brothers, the descendants of Esau, who live in Seir. We turned away from the Arabah road, which comes up from Elath and Ezion-geber, and traveled along the road of the Wilderness of Moab.","from":22},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Joshua and all Israel with him moved on from Libnah to Lachish. They laid siege to it and fought against it.","from":19},{"book":"1KI","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then David rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David.","from":20},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":41,"verseEnd":41,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As for the rest of the acts of Solomon—all that he did, as well as his wisdom—are they not written in the Book of the Acts of Solomon?","from":18},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":43,"verseEnd":43,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Solomon rested with his fathers and was buried in the city of his father David. And his son Rehoboam reigned in his place.","from":20},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As for the rest of the acts of Rehoboam, along with all that he did, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?","from":18}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"23-29":{"p