ses":4},{"base":"H2574","lemma":"חֲמָת","tr":"cha·mat","gloss":"Hamath","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":35},{"base":"H0657","lemma":"אֶ֫פֶס","tr":"e·phes","gloss":"end","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":44},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":877},{"base":"H0573","lemma":"אֲמִתַּי","tr":"a·mit·tay","gloss":"Amittai","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","tr":"ma·lakh","gloss":"to reign","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":348},{"base":"H8478","lemma":"תַּחַת","tr":"ta·chat","gloss":"underneath: under","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":505},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":820}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":13,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But the LORD was gracious to Israel and had compassion on them, and He turned toward them because of His covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. And to this day, the LORD has been unwilling to destroy them or cast them from His presence.","from":27},{"book":"DEU","chapter":32,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For the LORD will vindicate His people and have compassion on His servants when He sees that their strength is gone and no one remains, slave or free.","from":26},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and had gathered men to himself. When David killed the Zobaites, Rezon captained a band of raiders and went to Damascus, where they settled and gained control.","from":28},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The latter five came as allies to the Valley of Siddim (that is, the Salt Sea).","from":25},{"book":"GEN","chapter":38,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But Er, Judahʼs firstborn, was wicked in the sight of the Lord; so the Lordput him to death.","from":24},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The LORD said, “I have indeed seen the affliction of My people in Egypt. I have heard them crying out because of their oppressors, and I am aware of their sufferings.","from":26},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And now the cry of the Israelites has reached Me, and I have seen how severely the Egyptians are oppressing them.","from":26},{"book":"EXO","chapter":32,"verse":32,"verseEnd":33,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Yet now, if You would only forgive their sin.... But if not, please blot me out of the book that You have written.” The LORD replied to Moses, “Whoever has sinned against Me, I will blot out of My book.","from":27}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}